ff, and then go there sort of thing.<br /> <br /> We live in a world where destination is an external thing, when there are pilgramages where destination is a state of mind. There are journeys, where all you do is go around in circles, time and time again. and the only thing that changes each time is you.<br /> <br /> The video makes a point-that the destination is not a case of arriving to, but a case of being-of being wiser, more aware, more themselves, of fulfilling that which is one's self, rather than what other people tell it them to be, this plateau outside of themselves.<br /> <br /> THe Promethean is a human in embryo. The fullest expression of it is human. It is not a thing one can do by checking off things on a list, though it can be perceived as such. They learn to love, they learn to hate, they learn to sing and dance and they learn to cry and break. It is a spiritual journey, ultimately, one where destination is a state of mind, where there is no arrival but becoming, where you pass by where you started and realize that you are not the same shallow, empty thing that passed by here the first time.<br /> <br /> The video's point is that actualization does not come from what the world tells you to be and do, but what the fire within tells you change into. You'll never get there, standing still, merely being-you have to go and live, to take chances like snogging a stranger or diving off of a cliff or getting into a fight or being scared of something.<br /> <br /> Life is not a pilgramage, in the sense that life is a place trying to get somewhere. But life is a journey, in the sense that we travel, and change, and become.<br /> <br /> Destination is a state of mind. Drift along for the ride.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,